\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 The sound of gunfire and running water masked Halo\'92s footsteps; if he\'92d assaulted Sarah\'92s policewoman silently, he would almost certainly have finished her. Instead, the frustration of constant sideshows along his hero\'92s journey to the inmost cave, and the claiming of the elixir of Sarah\'92s blood had him growling like an amateur. \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The policewoman turned on him; he struck the back of her weapon hand, once, precisely, making her fingers spring open. He\'92d meant to seize the gun but succeeded only in assisting it to skitter across the flagstones and over the lips of the nearest pond. Fat orange fish fled to the farther reaches of their pond and held council.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Halo struck with his knife and cut deep into empty space. Hayley shifted off the line of attack, turning her body to meet him at an angle. He jabbed at her eyes, but she met him with her lead hand, keeping the other up and open. His arm was dragged across his body and her elbow swiftly opened the skin over his cheekbone with a short, heavy hit. The knife jumped from his fingers and clattered across the flagstones. Halo was pleased; he no longer felt the need to be polite.\
Hayley felt Halo\'92s knee in her thigh, deadening the muscle to the bone. She grunted through it and snapped her hand down across his incoming forearm, making his fingers flutter. He landed a hammer-fist on her collarbone; she stumbled.\
Halo closed on her. Hayley grabbed him by a sleeve and a lapel, drew him forward onto his toes, and tapped his ankle. As he over-balanced, she turned in with her hip under his belt, and threw him. Before he slammed on the floor, he slapped the stone, rolled and came to his feet. With her thigh all pins and needles , she tried to grapple him again. He landed a blow on her shoulder; the next sent her stumbling. Halo seized her, dragged her to the pond, and pushed her head back over the water. Both hands found her throat. She went for his arms and fingers with defensive exploration for weaknesses. Cold lapped at her hair, then her ears. Her vision went grey.\
There was blood in the water. Hayley\'92s mind went red with panic, but she couldn\'92t feel where she\'92d been cut.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

